&lt;h2 id=&#34;-demo&#34;&gt;📦 Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can see the latest build of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://checkmate-demo.bluewavelabs.ca/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Checkmate&lt;/a&gt; in action. The username is &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:uptimedemo@demo.com&#34; &gt;uptimedemo@demo.com&lt;/a&gt; and the password is Demouser1! (just a note that we update the demo server from time to time, so if it doesn&amp;rsquo;t work for you, please ping us on the Discussions channel).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;-users-guide&#34;&gt;🔗 User&amp;rsquo;s guide
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Usage instructions can be found &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.checkmate.so/checkmate-2.1&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. It&amp;rsquo;s still WIP and some of the information there might be outdated as we continuously add features weekly. Rest assured, we are doing our best! :)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;-installation&#34;&gt;🛠️ Installation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;See installation instructions in &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.checkmate.so/checkmate-2.1/users-guide/quickstart&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Checkmate documentation portal&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alternatively, you can also use &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coolify.io/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Coolify&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://elest.io/open-source/checkmate&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Elestio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;./charts/helm/checkmate/INSTALLATION.md&#34; &gt;K8s&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.pikapods.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Pikapods&lt;/a&gt; to quickly spin off a Checkmate instance. If you would like to monitor your server infrastructure, you&amp;rsquo;ll need &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/bluewave-labs/capture&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Capture agent&lt;/a&gt;. Capture repository also contains the installation instructions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;-translations&#34;&gt;🏁 Translations
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you would like to use Checkmate in your language, please &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://poeditor.com/join/project/lRUoGZFCsJ&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;go to this page&lt;/a&gt; and register for the language you would like to translate Checkmate to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;-performance&#34;&gt;🚀 Performance
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to extensive optimizations, Checkmate operates with an exceptionally small memory footprint, requiring minimal memory and CPU resources. Here’s the memory usage of a Node.js instance running on a server that monitors 323 servers every minute:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37e04a75-d83a-488f-b25c-025511b492c9&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;image&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can see the memory footprint of MongoDB and Redis on the same server (398Mb and 15Mb) for the same amount of servers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b469e85-e675-4040-a162-3f24c1afc751&#34;
	
	
	
