    &gt;Aryaman&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/mertssmnoglu&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Mert&lt;/a&gt; helping individuals and businesses monitor their infra and servers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pride ourselves on building strong connections with contributors at every level. Despite being a young project, Checkmate has already earned 6000+ stars and attracted 80+ contributors from around the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our repo is starred by employees from &lt;strong&gt;Google, Microsoft, Intel, Cisco, Tencent, Electronic Arts, ByteDance, JP Morgan Chase, Deloitte, Accenture, Foxconn, Broadcom, China Telecom, Barclays, Capgemini, Wipro, Cloudflare, Dassault Systèmes and NEC&lt;/strong&gt;, so don’t hold back — jump in, contribute and learn with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s how you can contribute:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol start=&#34;0&#34;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Star this repo :)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/bluewave-labs/Checkmate/blob/develop/CONTRIBUTING.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Contributor&amp;rsquo;s guideline&lt;/a&gt;. First timers are encouraged to check &lt;code&gt;good-first-issue&lt;/code&gt; tag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.checkmate.so/checkmate-2.1/developers-guide/general-project-structure&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;project structure&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://bluewavelabs.gitbook.io/checkmate/developers-guide/high-level-overview&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;high level overview&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read a detailed structure of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://deepwiki.com/bluewave-labs/Checkmate&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Checkmate&lt;/a&gt; if you would like to deep dive into the architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open an issue if you believe you&amp;rsquo;ve encountered a bug.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check for good-first-issue&amp;rsquo;s if you are a newcomer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make a pull request to add new features/make quality-of-life improvements/fix bugs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
